# Powertools Batch Processing

## Overview

`@aws-lambda-powertools/batch` provides a standard way to process SQS, Kinesis, and DynamoDB Streams events with automatic partial batch failure reporting. Use it instead of manually building `batchItemFailures` and classifying retryable errors.

## Dependencies

```bash
pnpm add @aws-lambda-powertools/batch
```

## SQS Batch Processor

```typescript
// src/functions/process-listings/handler.ts

import type { SQSEvent, SQSRecord, SQSBatchResponse } from "aws-lambda";
import { BatchProcessor, EventType, processPartialResponse } from "@aws-lambda-powertools/batch";
import { logger } from "@/shared/logger";
import { listingService } from "@/services/listing.service";

const processor = new BatchProcessor(EventType.SQS);

export const handler = async (event: SQSEvent): Promise<SQSBatchResponse> => {
  return processPartialResponse(event, processor, async (record: SQSRecord) => {
    const message = JSON.parse(record.body);
    const { eventType, payload } = message.data;

    logger.info({ eventType, messageId: record.messageId }, "Processing event");

    const result = await listingService.handleListingPublished(payload);

    if (!result.success) {
      if (result.error.isRetryable) {
        throw new Error(result.error.message); // Will be reported as batch item failure
      }
      throw new NonRetryableError(result.error.message, result.error.code);
    }
  });
};

class NonRetryableError extends Error {
  constructor(
    message: string,
    public readonly code: string
  ) {
    super(message);
    this.name = "NonRetryableError";
  }
}
```

## Retryable vs Non-Retryable

Powertools Batch reports failed items so SQS retries them. For non-retryable errors (e.g. validation), throw a custom error and use a **failure handler** to avoid retries, or let the message eventually go to the DLQ after max receives. To skip retries for non-retryable errors, throw with a specific name and handle in a custom `onFailure` callback (see Powertools docs) or use your existing SQS retry ladder and DLQ.

```typescript
// Prefer: throw for retryable, throw NonRetryableError for don't-retry
// NonRetryableError: message still returns in batchItemFailures by default;
// use reportBatchItemFailure: false in processPartialResponse options for non-retryable
// when supported, or document that non-retryable go to DLQ after max receives.
```

## DynamoDB Streams Batch Processor

```typescript
// src/functions/sync-to-opensearch/handler.ts

import type { DynamoDBStreamEvent, DynamoDBRecord } from "aws-lambda";
import { BatchProcessor, EventType, processPartialResponse } from "@aws-lambda-powertools/batch";
import { unmarshall } from "@aws-sdk/util-dynamodb";
import { opensearchService } from "@/services/opensearch.service";

const processor = new BatchProcessor(EventType.DynamoDBStreams);

export const handler = async (event: DynamoDBStreamEvent) => {
  return processPartialResponse(event, processor, async (record: DynamoDBRecord) => {
    if (record.eventName === "REMOVE") {
      const oldImage = record.dynamodb?.OldImage;
      if (oldImage) {
        const item = unmarshall(oldImage);
        await opensearchService.deleteDocument("listings", `${item.propertyId}-${item.listingId}`);
      }
      return;
    }

    const newImage = record.dynamodb?.NewImage;
    if (!newImage) return;

    const item = unmarshall(newImage);
    if (item.entityType !== "Listing") return;

    await opensearchService.indexDocument("listings", {
      id: `${item.propertyId}-${item.listingId}`,
      ...item,
    });
  });
};
```

## Kinesis Data Streams

Use `EventType.KinesisDataStreams` and a record handler that receives a KinesisStreamRecord. Same `processPartialResponse` pattern; failed records are reported for Kinesis checkpointing.

## Integration with Error Classification

Keep using your existing `AppError` and `isRetryable` logic inside the record handler. Throw for retry (message reappears), throw `NonRetryableError` (or similar) for business/validation failures so you can log and optionally avoid retries via DLQ routing or failure callback.

## Conventions

- Use `processPartialResponse` for all SQS/DynamoDB Streams/Kinesis handlers
- Throw to report a record as failed (batch item failure)
- Classify errors as retryable vs non-retryable; use DLQ for non-retryable after max receives
- Keep record handler logic pure (no side effects except the intended processing)
- Test with mixed success/failure batches (see `testing.mdc`)

## Anti-Patterns

- Manually building `batchItemFailures` when Powertools Batch can do it
- Swallowing errors inside the record handler (always throw on failure)
- Forgetting to enable `reportBatchItemFailures` on the SQS event source in CDK

**See also:** `sqs-processing.mdc`, `error-handling.mdc`, `testing.mdc`, `lambda-handlers.mdc`
